{
  "id": "COMPOUND:41664 - PROTEIN:2333",
  "verbalization": "Cytisine, N-formyl-, appears to be a target of multiple entities that ultimately lead to Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3. This suggests a potential pathway where Cytisine, through its interaction with HCT-8 or Conferol, influences the activity of Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3. The evidence indicates that Cytisine may act as a modulator of the downstream enzyme, possibly by altering the activity of upstream targets like HCT-8 or Conferol. The shared involvement of 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol in these relationships suggests a common mechanism, possibly involving the regulation of cellular processes through the modulation of these enzymes. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, where Cytisine may exert its effects through a series of interconnected targets, ultimately influencing the activity of Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3.",
